Vex CLI Study Timer @VERSION@ (Linux, @ARCH@)
=============================================

Thank you for downloading the prebuilt Linux build. This archive contains a
statically linked `vex-timer` binary: it has no shared-library dependencies
and runs on any Linux distribution (Debian, Ubuntu, Fedora, RHEL, Arch,
openSUSE, Alpine, ...) on this architecture, as long as the kernel is new
enough to run the toolchain that produced it (any supported kernel is fine).

Contents
--------

    vex-timer                 the program
    share/man/man1/vex-timer.1.gz   the vex-timer(1) manual page
    LICENSE                   the MIT license text
    INSTALL.txt               this file

Run without installing
----------------------

    tar -xzf vex-timer-@VERSION@-linux-@ARCH@.tar.gz
    cd vex-timer-@VERSION@-linux-@ARCH@
    ./vex-timer -s 4 -t 25 -b 5

The archive preserves the executable bit; if it was lost in transit, restore
it with `chmod +x vex-timer`.

Install onto the system (optional)
----------------------------------

Copy the binary and manual page into /usr/local (or any PREFIX you like):

    sudo install -m 755 vex-timer /usr/local/bin/vex-timer
    sudo install -m 644 share/man/man1/vex-timer.1.gz /usr/share/man/man1/vex-timer.1.gz

Then run `vex-timer` from anywhere and read the manual with
`man vex-timer`. Remove both files again to uninstall.

Optional runtime helpers
------------------------

- `aplay` (package `alsa-utils`) plays the synthesized chiptune alarms.
  Without it the timer falls back to the terminal bell.
- `notify-send` (package `libnotify-bin` on Debian/Ubuntu, `libnotify` on
  Fedora/Arch) sends desktop notifications at phase transitions. Disable
  them with `--no-notify`.

Verify the download (optional)
------------------------------

The release page publishes a SHA256SUMS file covering every artifact:

    sha256sum -c --ignore-missing SHA256SUMS

Other download options
----------------------

The same release page also offers:

- `vex-timer-@VERSION@-linux-@ARCH@.AppImage` - single-file executable,
  `chmod +x` it and run; nothing to install.
- `vex-timer_@VERSION@_@DEB_ARCH@.deb` - for Debian, Ubuntu, Mint, Pop!_OS,
  and other apt distributions: `sudo apt install ./vex-timer_@VERSION@_@DEB_ARCH@.deb`
- `vex-timer-@VERSION@-1.@RPM_ARCH@.rpm` - for Fedora, RHEL, openSUSE, and
  other rpm distributions: `sudo rpm -i vex-timer-@VERSION@-1.@RPM_ARCH@.rpm`
  (or `sudo dnf install ./vex-timer-@VERSION@-1.@RPM_ARCH@.rpm`)
- `vex-timer-@VERSION@-linux-@ARCH@` - the bare binary, for scripted
  downloads: `chmod +x vex-timer-@VERSION@-linux-@ARCH@ && ./vex-timer-@VERSION@-linux-@ARCH@ --help`

Project home: https://github.com/E-Vex/vex-cli-study-timer
